Task: Employee Management System using Spring
Boot and CrudRepository
Objective
Develop a Spring Boot application to manage Employee records using CrudRepository. Implement
all major CRUD operations provided by CrudRepository.
Scenario
A company wants to maintain employee information in a database. The HR department should be
able to add, view, update, delete, count, and verify employee records.
Entity Class: Employee
employeeId, employeeName, department, salary
Repository Interface
public interface EmployeeRepository extends CrudRepository {}
1. Add Single Employee
CrudRepository Method: save()
2. Add Multiple Employees
CrudRepository Method: saveAll()
3. View Employee By Id
CrudRepository Method: findById()
4. View All Employees
CrudRepository Method: findAll()
5. Check Employee Exists
CrudRepository Method: existsById()
6. Count Total Employees
CrudRepository Method: count()
7. Update Employee Details
CrudRepository Method: save()
8. Delete Employee By Id
CrudRepository Method: deleteById()
9. Delete Employee Record
CrudRepository Method: delete()
10. Delete Multiple Employees
CrudRepository Method: deleteAll(Iterable)
11. Delete All Employees
CrudRepository Method: deleteAll()
Classes Required
Employee, EmployeeRepository, EmployeeService, EmployeeServiceImpl, EmployeeController,
SpringBootCrudRepositoryApplication